xhausted account or model family until its reset: a job that stops at a subscription usage limit records the limit (in the controller database, so a restart keeps it), and the pool answers `limited` to any candidate whose role runs on that account or family (a whole-account session or weekly limit blocks every role; an Opus or Sonnet limit blocks only roles on that family, and a role with no model, which runs the CLI default, is blocked by any limit). A limited candidate takes no slot and reserves no demand, so lower classes are not held back. The block ends at the reset time the CLI reported; when it reported none the first pause is 30 minutes and each further stop with no reset doubles it up to 4 hours, starting over once a job succeeds; a reset time further away than 8 days is clamped. Running jobs are never killed for a limit. Deterministic scanners and the merger use no model and are unaffected. A daily dollar cap works the same way at the same gate: the pool answers `budget` to a candidate whose role cap or the repo cap is reached, and that candidate takes no slot and reserves no demand. A job that already holds a slot keeps it and finishes.\n332:8. **Open or update a draft PR** with ard's own `Closes #<issue>`, the agent summary quoted and neutralised (`committer.NeutraliseRefs`, then marker and mention defusing), the test result and links to `worker-<role>.md`, the logs and the job id. Reviewers are chosen by `config.SelectReviewers`: the candidates are the role's `reviewers` (a list that only narrows), or every reviewer role when it is unset or empty, and each candidate's `when:` still decides. A `when:` matches when any path changed between the merge base of the config commit and the pushed head matches a `paths` entry, or a listed triage role ran (closed `done`, or its `ard:triage:<role>:done` label; `needs-human` does not count). Paths are case-sensitive and anchored at the repo root: `web/` is a directory, anything else a doublestar glob, so `**/go.mod` matches a root `go.mod` and `go.mod` only the root one; `.ard/` and `.ard-input/` paths are never selectable. Any `review:<role>` the lead deferred or the worker's own `next` lists is added regardless of `when:`, limited to roles that exist, and requested only when the tests did not fail. Selection is monotonic: each run recomputes from the whole PR diff and close-out only adds labels, so earlier requests stay and newly matching reviewers are added. When the head or git is unavailable, path rules fail open. If no reviewer is selected the PR stays a draft (the loop logs `worker.no_reviewers`). The PR stays a draft; the merger marks it ready. A job that has pushed always gets its draft PR, even when it then ends in `ard:needs-human` or a failure, so pushed work is never left without one.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xs8s56SSu2wKaFM3smRoHm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
